# Copy to scripts/.env, then run: sudo ./scripts/deploy-debian.sh
# Leave empty to keep PostgreSQL's current data directory (Debian's default
# on a fresh install: /var/lib/postgresql/<version>/main).
# To use an external volume, mount it first and configure its mount in /etc/fstab.
# Use an absolute path to a subdirectory on that volume, for example:
# POSTGRES_DATA_DIR=/mnt/balnana-volume/postgresql
# Optional: require this exact path to be a mounted filesystem. The data directory
# must be at or below it. The script checks it before installation/initialization;
# systemd uses RequiresMountsFor and AssertPathIsMountPoint at service startup.
# POSTGRES_VOLUME_MOUNT=/mnt/balnana-volume
# Paths containing spaces may be enclosed in single or double quotes.
# Existing data is NOT moved. An empty target gets a new database cluster;
# reruns reuse the cluster at that path. Nonempty non-PostgreSQL targets fail.
POSTGRES_DATA_DIR=
POSTGRES_VOLUME_MOUNT=
